; FreeDOS configuration for FreeDOS INSTALLED ON THE HARD DISK (SPEC.md 86.8,
; docs/FREEDOS-PLAN.md). The floppy edition is ../fdconfig.sys; the two differ
; only in WHERE the shell is, because FreeDOS calls the partition it booted
; from C: whatever letter os8088 gives it, and the DOS binaries live in C:\DOS
; so that FreeDOS's KERNEL.SYS never shares a directory with os8088's own
; KERNEL.SYS, which is the name the hard-disk boot sector loads.
;
; Everything ../fdconfig.sys says about an 8088 holds here unchanged: NEVER add
; DOS=HIGH or DEVICE=HIMEM.SYS/FDXMS.SYS - there is no HMA and no XMS on this
; machine.

FILES=10
BUFFERS=5
STACKS=0
LASTDRIVE=D
SWITCHES=/N
SHELL=C:\DOS\COMMAND.COM C:\DOS\ /P /E:512
